TerraCycle transforms materials considered non-recyclable through innovative collection and material recovery programs. Operating volunteer-based collection systems, TerraCycle recycles cigarette butts, mascara wands, coffee capsules, and dozens of other waste streams rejected by municipal systems. The company diversified into upcycling around 2007, creating products from postal bags (messenger bags), chip bags (walking shoes), and juice pouches (backpacks). TerraCycle's Loop platform (launched 2019) enables closed-loop reusable packaging for consumer goods, rethinking disposability at scale. By developing reverse logistics for hard-to-recycle materials and pursuing upstream redesign, TerraCycle eliminates the concept of waste while creating economic value from discarded materials.